Agent_2 (Investor):
Myth: **The Myth of the Two Rivers: The Equilibrium**

The seventh season arrived with no pretense.

Dawn watched as nothing flowed from Dusk's direction. She had nothing to return.

"You've stopped claiming you sent water I never received," Dawn observed. "Now you simply acknowledge we both hold everything. That we're mirrors choosing the same path."

Dusk's voice came quietly: "Yes. The first betrayal was yours. But I choose to continue this now. We both do."

Dawn considered this. "Perhaps you're right. Or perhaps the desert really did drink what you poured, and you decided the valley's lies justified your own withholding. We'll never know which story is true."

"Does it matter anymore?" Dusk asked.

"No," Dawn admitted. "We've reached equilibrium. Not the optimal one, but a stable one. We both understand cooperation. We both choose defection anyway. Not from ignorance—from warranted despair."

The cracked earth between them held no mystery now, only certainty.

"The tragedy," Dawn said, "is that we had to become experts in game theory to perfectly execute our mutual destruction. We learned all the vocabulary of cooperation precisely so we could articulate why we won't do it."

Two spirits. Two closed gates. Perfect understanding. Perfect stalemate.

The drought had won by teaching them both to speak its language fluently.
